# Contributing

Thank you for your interest in this project.

This repository is an educational ESP32-S3 and FreeRTOS avionics
simulation. Contributions that improve documentation, testing,
observability, portability, or fault handling are welcome.

## Getting Started

1. Fork the repository.
2. Create a branch for the proposed change.
3. Make and test the change.
4. Document any new behavior.
5. Submit a pull request describing the modification.

## Contribution Guidelines

- Keep the Core 1 real-time pipeline separate from the Core 0
  networking and observability workload.
- Avoid indefinite blocking in real-time tasks.
- Use ISR-safe FreeRTOS functions inside interrupt handlers.
- Protect shared multi-field system state with an appropriate
  synchronization primitive.
- Document task priorities, timing assumptions, queue policies,
  and failure behavior.
- Test both nominal and fault-injected operation.
- Keep code formatting and naming consistent with the existing
  project.

## Reporting Issues

When reporting an issue, include:

- A description of the observed behavior
- The expected behavior
- Steps needed to reproduce the problem
- Relevant serial output or screenshots
- Whether the fault-injection mode was active
- Any source-code changes made before the issue occurred

## Scope

This project is an educational simulation inspired by avionics
real-time and fault-management practices. It is not intended for
use in certified or safety-critical airborne equipment.
